IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr-definitions`

-- TESTS for mlr-core.l4 and mlr-definitions.l4 (regs 3 to 7 of S.I. 2017/692).
-- Every expected value below is written by hand from the text of the Regulations as rendered
-- in uksi-2017-692.txt (a converter's plain-text rendering, not the official text); none is
-- copied from the encoding's output.  Each answer is JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE or NOTHING; NOTHING
-- is "the text does not answer", never FALSE.

§ `Tests: the core`

-- reg 1(2): "These Regulations come into force on 26th June 2017."  (Date is day, month, year.)
#ASSERT `reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force` EQUALS Date 26 6 2017
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 1(2) the date these Regulations came into force` EQUALS Date 27 6 2017)
-- regs 27(1)(b), 27(7E), 64C(4), 64G(1)(b): £800.
#ASSERT `the transfer threshold of 800 pounds sterling` EQUALS 800

§ `Tests: reg 2, prescribed regulations`

#ASSERT `reg 2 these Regulations are prescribed for the purposes of` EQUALS "sections 168(4)(b) (appointment of persons to carry out investigations in particular cases) and 402(1)(b) (power of the FCA to institute proceedings for certain other offences) of the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000"

§ `Tests: reg 3(1), terms that stand for a public body`

#ASSERT `reg 3(1) the FCA` EQUALS `the Financial Conduct Authority`
#ASSERT `reg 3(1) the Commissioners` EQUALS `the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`
#ASSERT `reg 3(1) Department for the Economy` EQUALS `the Department for the Economy in Northern Ireland`
#ASSERT `reg 3(1) the NCA` EQUALS `the National Crime Agency`
#ASSERT `reg 3(1) the PRA` EQUALS `the Prudential Regulation Authority`
-- the FCA is not the PRA
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 3(1) the FCA` EQUALS `the Prudential Regulation Authority`)

